# Reference assets dropped in the repo root by a3obReference (Save Selection as Body/
# Skeleton). These are Bohemia's, published under ADPL-SA — non-commercial, Arma/DayZ only,
# share-alike — which is incompatible with this repo's MIT licence. Anchored to the root on
# purpose: docs/specs/2026-07-20-skinning-panel-design.md has them ship from
# assets/references/ instead, alongside their own LICENCE and attribution.
#
# This root rule stays even now that assets/references/ is tracked: a3obReference's Save
# Selection as... still writes new Body/Skeleton saves to the repo root first, and those
# must keep landing here untracked. assets/references/ is the shipped, licensed home for
# the two prepared files the plugin ships with; it is intentionally not covered by this
# anchored (root-only) pattern.
/dayz_*.ma
